# 7. REPOSITION THE OFFER — WHY ADVIBE STUDIOS IS DIFFERENT

The page must clearly explain why our programme is different from ordinary AI video courses.

Do not rely on vague claims such as “the best AI course,” “revolutionary training,” or “unlimited success.”

Our differentiation should be based on the actual structure of the programme, the experience of the instructors, the work of our agency, and the learning environment.

The most important differentiators are:

## A. We are an agency that teaches

Advibe Studios is a creative agency that applies AI tools to real business content needs.

We are not positioning ourselves as people who only watch tutorials and then teach other people to do the same.

Our agency work gives us practical context for understanding what businesses need, what makes content effective, how creative work is delivered, and where AI tools fit into real production workflows.

Explain this distinction in simple language.

Make it clear that the course is informed by real agency practice, without implying that every lesson or tool has been independently proven to guarantee commercial results.

## B. An instructor combination

Present the instructor combination as an important reason to choose the programme.

Inspect the existing founder and instructor biographies. Use verified information to explain what each instructor brings to the training and why their combined experience is valuable.

Do not invent credentials, years of experience, qualifications, or achievements.

Make the presentation visual, personal, and easy to understand. Prospective students should understand who will teach them, what they bring, and how the instructors complement each other.

## C. Two weeks of intensive, hands-on training

This is not positioned as a course where students simply receive prerecorded lessons and are left alone.

The programme is a two-week hands-on intensive.

Emphasise that students are expected to practise, create, experiment, and learn by doing.

Explain the practical difference:

- Watching a video demonstrates what someone else can do.
- Guided practice helps a student learn how to do it themselves.
- Feedback and iteration help them identify what needs improvement.
- Repeated practice helps them build a more reliable creative workflow.

Use only the teaching formats and support actually included in the programme. Do not promise individual coaching, live sessions, or specific feedback frequency unless confirmed.

## D. A learning community

Explain the value of learning alongside other people.

The community should be presented as a place to exchange ideas, ask questions where supported, share progress, learn from different approaches, and remain engaged while practising.

Do not promise a particular response time or permanent access unless the actual programme provides it.

## E. Real business context and credibility

We are an agency with active business work.

For now, **CirclesFundMe should be the only company presented as an active client or company partner in this section**.

We have worked with CirclesFundMe and generated thousands of messaging conversations around its business.

Use the verified facts available in the project to explain the nature of the work and its relevance to AI-powered creative production and business communication.

Do not imply that CirclesFundMe endorses the course, guarantees student outcomes, or formally endorses Advibe Studios unless that relationship is explicitly authorised and verified.

Do not add other companies to the active-partner showcase merely to make the page look more impressive.

## F. Practical outcomes, not just access to information

The programme should be presented around what students learn to do.

Focus on practical capabilities such as creating video content, developing creative concepts, producing visuals, refining content, and building a repeatable process.

Use the existing curriculum to determine the exact deliverables and skills taught.

Make the outcome tangible without guaranteeing income, employment, viral videos, clients, or business growth.

